# Environment Variables

This document lists all environment variables used by Prompt Perfector.

## Required Variables

### Supabase Connection

```env
# Supabase project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Supabase anonymous (public) key
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
```

## Optional Variables

### Analytics

```env
# PostHog project API key (for analytics)
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...

# PostHog host (defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com)
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
```

## Edge Function Secrets

These are set in Supabase Edge Function settings, NOT in .env files:

```
# Comma-separated list of admin email addresses
ADMIN_EMAILS=admin@example.com,owner@example.com

# These are automatically provided by Supabase:
SUPABASE_URL
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
```

## Setting Variables

### Local Development

Create a `.env.local` file (gitignored):

```env
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=your-posthog-key
```

### Vercel Deployment

1. Go to Project Settings → Environment Variables
2. Add each variable with the appropriate value
3. Set scope (Production, Preview, Development)

### Netlify Deployment

1. Go to Site Settings → Build & Deploy → Environment
2. Add each variable
3. Redeploy to apply changes

## Security Notes

- Never commit `.env.local` or any file containing secrets
- `VITE_` prefix makes variables available in client-side code
- Only use `VITE_` for truly public keys (like Supabase anon key)
- Keep service role keys in Edge Function secrets only
